{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:bed595024dbcaf30","name":"P-38 Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-bed595024dbcaf30","title":"P-38 Starfighter","revision":18771,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:42:27Z","sha256":"9cc2f949ae81b4fb2281750117a4a4057c7f8597b03ee3d27d4a6343650734b1","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18771","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=P-38%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-bed595024dbcaf30","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Prior to the occupation of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utapau"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utapau","referenceId":"reference:236cdadb0b901b45"}," by the Separatists during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", the port administrator at the time, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tion Medon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tion_Medon?action=edit&redlink=1"},", instructed that the planetary militia was to hide its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," fleet in the multitude of caves and recessed sinkholes that covered the planetary surface. With the arrival of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Obi-Wan Kenobi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Obi-Wan_Kenobi","referenceId":"reference:6e84377ee76928db"},", the hidden ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," (including several squadrons of P-38s) were readied for battle.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When the Republic invasion force landed, the fighters were sent out on sorties in support of clone-piloted ",{"tag":"a","children":["ARC-170s"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/ARC-170s"},". Although the P-38 Starfighter was the standard model available to pilots during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", several variants also saw use. The most influential variant was the P-38 \"Jenta.\" The \"Jenta\" was the primary ground assault craft of the militia, and it proved invaluable when used to neutralize Droid forces on the ground, thanks to its fin-guided Ion Bombs.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The P-38 was specifically manufactured to hold ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utai","referenceId":"reference:e74913a98df69c0d"}," pilots, rather than the taller ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pau'ans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pau%27ans"}," who ruled the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utapau"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utapau","referenceId":"reference:236cdadb0b901b45"},". With some effort, the Starfighter can be modified to suit Medium characters, but this can be costly given the rarity of spare parts outside ",{"tag":"a","children":["Utapau"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Utapau","referenceId":"reference:236cdadb0b901b45"}," space. Smaller ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ewoks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ewoks"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jawas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jawas"},", find the fighter much more comfortable.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Foremost among the P-38's strengths is it's advanced sensor system, which grants a +2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," checks made to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Sensors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Sensors","referenceId":"reference:1bf2e88f5409e504"},". The ship is also outfitted with specialized jamming equipment that is keyed to affect Droid sensors and avionics. When the jammers are employerd, a P-38 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," gains a +2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus on attack rolls against automated craft, such as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vulture Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vulture_Droid","referenceId":"reference:222b298d9ab6355b"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Tri-Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Tri-Fighter","referenceId":"reference:a43f8b93305b7f0a"}," employed by the Trade Federation. The jammers affect only Droid-controlled spacecraft within a 5-square radius.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The \"Jenta\" variant of the P-38 carries the same equipment as the standard fighter, but with the addition of six fin-guided Ion Bombs. Because of their primitive fin-stabilized guidance system, the bombs are usable only in an atmosphere, and attacks with them take a -4 penalty. On impact, they create a strong Ion field that deals 5d10 points of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion"}," damage within a 20-square (",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Character_Scale"},") radius.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["P-38 Starfighter Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"h